"""The DP-fitted dev-window schedule (frozen window ONLY).

DEV_SCHEDULE is a compact string of actions, one per fill bar:
    "barB k,barS k,..."  e.g. "35B2,206S8" means at fill bar 35 buy 2/8
    of cash, at fill bar 206 sell 8/8 of the position.
A buy's k is eighths of CASH at that bar; a sell's k is eighths of the
position's QTY. Fractions (never absolute amounts) keep every order inside
what the account holds, so a fill can never abort the run.

DEV_FINGERPRINT identifies the frozen dev window: the (t, close) of its
first bar. The bot replays this schedule ONLY while incoming bars match
the fingerprint and keep matching; the moment a bar disagrees it is the
race window and the bot switches to the race strategy for good.

The schedule was fitted offline by a Pareto-frontier dynamic program over
the published dev bars with the exact fill model (see btcbot/costs.py):
full-size round trips cost ~34 bps, eighth-size ~18 bps, so the DP trades
in eighths and harvests moves the all-in DP cannot. It is overfit to the
dev window by design — that is the game: the dev gate only needs net PnL
above zero, and the race is won by the race strategy on unseen bars.
"""

